    <desc>Choose one of about 240 color schemes, make your own, or make the background transparent.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Color schemes</title>

<p>Each <link xref="pref-profiles">profile</link> has its own colors. To
  change them:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item><item><p>In the <gui>Profiles</gui> group, click the profile you want to change. Its settings open on a page of their own.</p></item>
<item><p>Change the settings in the <gui>Colors</gui> group. They apply at once.</p></item>
</steps>

  <section id="schemes">
    <title>Color schemes</title>
    <p>Choose one of about 240 schemes, such as Gruvbox, Nord, Dracula,
    Solarized or Tango, in <gui>Color Scheme</gui>. Type a few letters to find
    one. A scheme sets the text, background and palette colors. Schemes that
    have a light and a dark variant switch with the light or dark style of the
    system.</p>
    <p>To make your own schemes, put <file>.palette</file> files into the
    folder that <gui style="button">Open Folder</gui> next to <gui>Your Own
    Color Schemes</gui> opens, <file>~/.local/share/pano-terminal/schemes</file>.
    They appear in the list at once.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="custom">
    <title>Colors of your own</title>
    <p>Set <gui>Color Scheme</gui> to <gui>Custom</gui> to choose the colors of
    the profile yourself:</p>
    <terms>
      <item>
        <title><gui>Use Colors from System Style</gui></title>
        <p>Use the text and background colors of the light or dark style of
        the system.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title><gui>Use Colors from Scheme</gui></title>
        <p>Start from one of the built-in combinations of text and background
        color, such as <gui>Black on white</gui> or <gui>Solarized dark</gui>.
        The <gui>Override</gui> rows below it set the text and background, bold
        text, cursor and highlight colors one by one.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title><gui>Palette</gui></title>
        <p>Choose the 16 colors that programs use for colored output, from a
        built-in palette or one by one.</p>
      </item>
    </terms>
    <note>
      <p>Terminals traditionally offer 16 colors, which you can change here.
      <app>Pano Terminal</app> also supports 256 colors and “true color” with
      over 16 million colors, which programs can use directly. If a change to
      the palette seems to have no effect, the program probably uses such
      colors.</p>
    </note>
  </section>

  <section id="opacity">
    <title>Transparent background</title>
    <p>Lower <gui>Background Opacity</gui> to let the desktop show through the
    background of the terminal. The text, the header bar and the tabs stay
    opaque.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="bold-color">
    <title>Bright colors for bold text</title>
    <p>Traditionally, terminals showed bold text in brighter colors too. Turn
    off <gui>Show Bold Text in Bright Colors</gui> to keep color and font
    weight apart, which suits schemes such as Solarized; turn it on for
    programs that expect the old behavior.</p>
  </section>

